From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JJ Eaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drama: a voice's reference rows are prefilled once and
 resumed from on later prompts

A referenced prompt's rows through its system message (instruction, transcripts, reference codes and its <|im_end|>) are the speech request's new prefix_rows, 0 for a plain prompt. Its prompt pass runs them in their own chunks of up to 128 rows, then the rest, so a pass that resumes after them runs exactly the chunks it skips; a plain prompt's passes are as before. After the chunk ending there, the backbone's whole DeltaNet state buffer, its attention k and v rows, position and chunk metadata, and the tower's k and v rows and position are copied to a cache entry keyed by the prompt rows [0, prefix_rows] in full (the last row is the tower's label for that chunk). A later request whose rows match restores the entry after both models' reset and starts its pass at prefix_rows. DRAMA_PREFIX_CACHE sets the entries kept (default 2, least recently used dropped; 0 turns the cache off); an entry takes about 152 MiB plus 46 KiB a prefix row, and a failed allocation or copy leaves no entry and never fails the request.
